        "original_id": "0b24cbea-8a8c-56bb-8b15-696c1fd8e1c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Minardi M190, Minardi M189B, Cosworth DFR V8 engine, Pirelli tyres\n- Companies: Pirelli & C. S.p.A., ChemChina\n- Places: Milan, Italy\n- Events: 1922 Milan Stock Exchange listing, early-season replacement in the first two races\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1922, Pirelli & C. S.p.A. was listed on the Milan Stock Exchange.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is a multinational company based in Milan, Italy.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is now an overseas subsidiary of the Chinese state-owned enterprise ChemChina.\n- For the season, the Minardi M189 was updated as the Minardi M189B.\n- The Minardi M189B was used for the first two races of the year before being replaced by the Minardi M190.\n- The Minardi M190 was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine.\n- The Minardi M190 ran on Pirelli tyres.",
